id=a52sxq_device_image_a52s
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: own device picture in Settings > About phone
author=kusti420
description=About phone shows a picture that Settings downloads from Samsung's SCPM server (DeviceImageManager$1, item 2) for a product code. unica/mods/device_image replaces the code with a fixed S26 Ultra one (SM-S948BZDGEUX), so the header showed an S26 Ultra with S Pen. This puts back the stock source, the phone's own ril.product_code (e.g. SM-A528BZKCSEB), so the server returns the A52s 5G picture in the phone's own colour. Falls back to SM-A528BZKCSEB when the property is empty. The cached /data/user_de/0/com.android.settings/files/DeviceImage.png is replaced on the next About phone visit once it is older than a day.
